ty","/arc-plc/washington/columbia-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and August to September came in under 90% of normal in 40 of those 75 years. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 16% of normal in June to July and 33% in May to June. So far in 2026, May to June stands at 41% and June to July at 32% on the middle of the grids. July to August is the driest pair at 1.34 inches normal, and November to December is the wettest at 5.69.</p>"}
